From: Loong <1031313955@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: airoha: tell a U-Boot loaded over the serial port

A U-Boot loaded into RAM over XMODEM -- to look at a board, back it up or
recover it -- went on to boot the system on flash like the one on flash
does, and saved the environment when a newer build refreshed the menu.
ramboot.c (in the package's src/) finds out at boot: BL2 leaves a FIP it
took over XMODEM in its memmap window, a FIP it loads from flash it does
not.  The "ramboot" command tells the boot scripts.
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-airoha/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-airoha/Makefile
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 obj-y	+= cpu.o
 obj-y	+= bootmenu-refresh.o
+obj-y	+= ramboot.o
 
 obj-$(CONFIG_TARGET_EN7523) += en7523/
 obj-$(CONFIG_TARGET_AN7581) += an7581/
